insert into public.sq_lorekeeper (term_id, is_active, grade_level, passage, question, choice_a, choice_b, choice_c, choice_d, correct_choice) values
  (1, true, 3, 'A plant has many parts. The root holds the plant in the soil and takes in water. The stem carries water up to the leaves. The leaves make food for the plant using sunlight.', 'Which part of the plant takes in water from the soil?', 'The leaf', 'The root', 'The flower', 'The stem', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, 'A plant has many parts. The root holds the plant in the soil and takes in water. The stem carries water up to the leaves. The leaves make food for the plant using sunlight.', 'What is the job of the stem?', 'To make food using sunlight', 'To hold the plant in the soil', 'To carry water up to the leaves', 'To attract insects', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Plants make their own food through a process called photosynthesis. They use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide from the air.', 'What three things do plants need to make food through photosynthesis?', 'Soil, water, and moonlight', 'Sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide', 'Fertilizer, water, and oxygen', 'Sunlight, salt, and carbon dioxide', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'What is the correct order of a plant''s life cycle?', 'Seedling → seed → plant → fruit', 'Seed → seedling → plant → fruit', 'Fruit → seed → plant → seedling', 'Plant → seed → fruit → seedling', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which plant part usually turns into a fruit after it is pollinated?', 'The root', 'The stem', 'The flower', 'The leaf', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Why do leaves need sunlight?', 'To grow taller stems', 'To make food for the plant', 'To attract more roots', 'To stop water from evaporating', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Animals can be grouped by how their bodies are covered. Some animals have scales, like fish. Some have feathers, like birds. Some have fur, like dogs and cats.', 'Which body covering do birds have?', 'Scales', 'Fur', 'Feathers', 'Shells', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Animals that lay eggs are called ___, while animals that give birth to live babies are ___.', 'mammals; oviparous', 'oviparous; viviparous', 'viviparous; oviparous', 'reptiles; amphibians', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'A fish lives its whole life in which habitat?', 'Land', 'Air', 'Water', 'Underground', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these animals is covered in scales?', 'A duck', 'A snake', 'A rabbit', 'A carabao', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'A butterfly starts as an egg, then becomes a caterpillar, then a chrysalis, and finally an adult butterfly. What is this process called?', 'Photosynthesis', 'Habitat change', 'Life cycle', 'Classification', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which animal gives birth to live young instead of laying eggs?', 'Chicken', 'Frog', 'Turtle', 'Dog', 'd'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Matter can be a solid, a liquid, or a gas. A solid keeps its own shape, like a rock. A liquid takes the shape of its container, like juice in a glass. A gas spreads out to fill any space, like air.', 'Why does juice take the shape of the glass it is poured into?', 'Because it is a solid', 'Because it is a liquid', 'Because it is a gas', 'Because it is heavy', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Matter can be a solid, a liquid, or a gas. A solid keeps its own shape, like a rock. A liquid takes the shape of its container, like juice in a glass. A gas spreads out to fill any space, like air.', 'Which state of matter always keeps its own shape?', 'Gas', 'Liquid', 'Solid', 'Steam', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'When you mix salt into water, what happens to the salt?', 'It disappears forever and cannot be brought back', 'It dissolves and mixes evenly into the water', 'It turns into a gas', 'It floats on top of the water', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these is an example of a gas?', 'Ice cube', 'Milk', 'The air we breathe', 'A wooden block', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'If you mix soil and water together and let it settle, what usually happens?', 'The soil completely dissolves like sugar', 'The soil sinks and separates from the water', 'The water turns into a gas', 'The mixture turns into a solid rock', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which property best describes a solid like a wooden block?', 'It flows and spreads out to fill any container', 'It has no fixed shape of its own', 'It keeps its own shape unless a force changes it', 'It is always invisible', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Weather tools help us measure the weather. A thermometer measures temperature. A rain gauge measures how much rain has fallen. An anemometer measures wind speed. A weather vane shows wind direction.', 'Which tool would you use to find out how fast the wind is blowing?', 'Thermometer', 'Rain gauge', 'Anemometer', 'Weather vane', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Weather tools help us measure the weather. A thermometer measures temperature. A rain gauge measures how much rain has fallen. An anemometer measures wind speed. A weather vane shows wind direction.', 'Which tool tells you which direction the wind is blowing?', 'Rain gauge', 'Weather vane', 'Thermometer', 'Anemometer', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which tool would you use to check how hot or cold it is outside?', 'Rain gauge', 'Anemometer', 'Thermometer', 'Weather vane', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Dark, thick clouds that often bring heavy rain are usually called what type of cloud?', 'Cirrus clouds', 'Cumulus clouds', 'Nimbus clouds', 'Stratus clouds', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'In the Philippines, what are the two main seasons called?', 'Spring and fall', 'Tag-init and tag-lamig', 'Tag-araw and tag-ulan', 'Wet and frozen', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'A rain gauge is most useful for measuring which of these?', 'How windy it is', 'How much rain fell in a day', 'How hot the sun is', 'Which way the clouds are moving', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Soil comes in different types. Clay soil holds water well but drains slowly. Sandy soil drains water quickly but does not hold nutrients well. Loamy soil is a mix that holds water and nutrients well, making it great for growing plants.', 'Which type of soil is best for growing most plants?', 'Clay soil', 'Sandy soil', 'Loamy soil', 'Rocky soil', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Soil comes in different types. Clay soil holds water well but drains slowly. Sandy soil drains water quickly but does not hold nutrients well. Loamy soil is a mix that holds water and nutrients well, making it great for growing plants.', 'Which type of soil lets water drain away the fastest?', 'Clay soil', 'Sandy soil', 'Loamy soil', 'Wet soil', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Rocks can be described by their properties. Which of these is a property of a rock?', 'Its favorite color', 'Its hardness and texture', 'Its ability to grow', 'Its name in Filipino', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which soil type is known for holding water but draining very slowly?', 'Sandy soil', 'Loamy soil', 'Clay soil', 'Rocky soil', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'A rock that feels rough and breaks easily probably has which properties?', 'Smooth and unbreakable', 'Rough texture and low hardness', 'Soft like a sponge', 'Liquid and see-through', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Farmers often use loamy soil to grow crops because it is best known for', 'Being the driest type of soil', 'Holding both water and nutrients well', 'Being made only of sand', 'Never needing sunlight', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Simple machines make work easier. A lever helps lift heavy things, like a seesaw. A wheel and axle helps things move, like a doorknob. A pulley uses a rope and wheel to lift objects, like a flagpole.', 'Which simple machine uses a rope and a wheel to lift things, like raising a flag?', 'Lever', 'Pulley', 'Wedge', 'Screw', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Simple machines make work easier. A lever helps lift heavy things, like a seesaw. A wheel and axle helps things move, like a doorknob. A pulley uses a rope and wheel to lift objects, like a flagpole.', 'A seesaw is an example of which simple machine?', 'Pulley', 'Wedge', 'Lever', 'Inclined plane', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which simple machine is a flat surface that slopes, used to help move heavy things up or down, like a ramp?', 'Inclined plane', 'Wheel and axle', 'Pulley', 'Lever', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'A doorknob turning to open a door is an example of which simple machine?', 'Wedge', 'Wheel and axle', 'Inclined plane', 'Pulley', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'An axe blade splitting wood is an example of which simple machine?', 'Wedge', 'Lever', 'Pulley', 'Wheel and axle', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'A screw is a simple machine that works like a twisted version of which other simple machine?', 'Pulley', 'Lever', 'Inclined plane', 'Wheel and axle', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Long ago, early Filipinos lived in small communities called barangays. Each barangay was led by a chief called a datu. Barangays often traded goods like rice, cloth, and gold with neighboring countries such as China.', 'What was the leader of a barangay called?', 'Datu', 'Hari', 'Punong barangay', 'Kapitan', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Long ago, early Filipinos lived in small communities called barangays. Each barangay was led by a chief called a datu. Barangays often traded goods like rice, cloth, and gold with neighboring countries such as China.', 'What kind of goods did early barangays trade with other countries?', 'Cars and machines', 'Rice, cloth, and gold', 'Books and paper', 'Electronics', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'The barangay system was an early form of what in the Philippines?', 'A school system', 'A community or settlement', 'A type of boat', 'A style of clothing', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Before the Spanish arrived, Filipino communities traded with which neighboring country?', 'China', 'Canada', 'Brazil', 'Egypt', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these best describes the role of a datu in a barangay?', 'A student in the barangay school', 'A trader who only sold cloth', 'The leader who guided the community', 'A visitor from another barangay', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Jose Rizal is remembered as a Filipino national hero mainly because he', 'Led a violent revolution against Spain', 'Wrote novels and inspired Filipinos through his writing and ideas', 'Was the first president of the Philippines', 'Invented the barangay system', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Andres Bonifacio is known in Philippine history for', 'Founding a group called the Katipunan to fight for independence', 'Writing the novel Noli Me Tangere', 'Building the first barangay', 'Inviting the Spanish to the Philippines', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which right below is a basic right that children have?', 'The right to skip all schoolwork', 'The right to be safe, cared for, and educated', 'The right to ignore family rules', 'The right to travel anywhere alone', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these is a responsibility a Grade 3 student has at school?', 'Following classroom rules and respecting others', 'Deciding the teacher''s lesson plan', 'Choosing not to attend class', 'Ignoring the class schedule', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'A responsibility a child has at home might be to', 'Help with simple chores like cleaning their room', 'Pay the family''s bills', 'Decide where the family will live', 'Manage the family business', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, 'People have needs and wants. Needs are things we must have to live, like food, water, and shelter. Wants are things that are nice to have but not necessary, like toys or candy.', 'Which of these is an example of a need, not a want?', 'A new toy', 'Clean water to drink', 'A video game', 'Candy', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, 'People have needs and wants. Needs are things we must have to live, like food, water, and shelter. Wants are things that are nice to have but not necessary, like toys or candy.', 'Which of these is an example of a want?', 'Shelter', 'Food', 'A new bicycle', 'Water', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'In a community''s economy, a farmer who grows rice to sell is acting as a', 'Consumer', 'Producer', 'Teacher', 'Datu', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'A person who buys goods from a market to use at home is acting as a', 'Producer', 'Farmer', 'Consumer', 'Trader only', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these is a natural structure, not a human-made one?', 'A bridge', 'A mountain', 'A school building', 'A road', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these is a human-made structure in a community?', 'A river', 'A forest', 'A market building', 'A hill', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Ana woke up early and saw dark clouds outside her window. She quickly grabbed her umbrella before leaving for school. On the way, it began to rain heavily, but Ana stayed dry.', 'Why did Ana bring her umbrella?', 'She saw dark clouds and expected rain', 'Her mother told her it was sunny', 'She wanted to use it as a toy', 'She forgot her raincoat', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Ana woke up early and saw dark clouds outside her window. She quickly grabbed her umbrella before leaving for school. On the way, it began to rain heavily, but Ana stayed dry.', 'What was the problem in the story, and how was it solved?', 'Ana was late for school, so she ran', 'It rained heavily, but Ana''s umbrella kept her dry', 'Ana lost her umbrella and got wet', 'Ana forgot her homework, so she went back home', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Ana woke up early and saw dark clouds outside her window. She quickly grabbed her umbrella before leaving for school. On the way, it began to rain heavily, but Ana stayed dry.', 'What is most likely to happen next if Ana did NOT bring her umbrella?', 'She would have gotten wet in the rain', 'The rain would have stopped early', 'She would have arrived at school faster', 'Nothing would have changed', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Miguel wanted to grow a garden. First, he prepared the soil. Next, he planted the seeds. Then he watered them every day. Finally, small green sprouts appeared.', 'What did Miguel do first when growing his garden?', 'He watered the seeds', 'He prepared the soil', 'He planted the seeds', 'He saw sprouts appear', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Miguel wanted to grow a garden. First, he prepared the soil. Next, he planted the seeds. Then he watered them every day. Finally, small green sprouts appeared.', 'What happened right after Miguel planted the seeds?', 'He prepared the soil', 'Sprouts appeared immediately', 'He watered them every day', 'He harvested the plants', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'A paragraph that explains the steps to bake a cake, in order, is an example of which text type?', 'Descriptive text', 'Time-order or procedural text', 'Persuasive text', 'Poetry', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'A paragraph that paints a picture with words, describing how a sunset looks and feels, is an example of which text type?', 'Procedural text', 'Explanatory text', 'Descriptive text', 'Persuasive text', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which sentence correctly joins two independent clauses with a coordinating conjunction?', 'Ana likes apples she also likes bananas.', 'Ana likes apples, and she also likes bananas.', 'Ana likes apples but bananas.', 'Ana, likes apples and bananas.', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'What is a coordinating conjunction used for in a compound sentence?', 'To start a new paragraph', 'To join two independent clauses', 'To describe a noun', 'To ask a question', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which word is a coordinating conjunction that can join two independent clauses?', 'quickly', 'and', 'happy', 'under', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these is a synonym for the word "happy"?', 'Sad', 'Angry', 'Joyful', 'Tired', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these is an antonym for the word "begin"?', 'Start', 'End', 'Continue', 'Open', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'The prefix "un-" in the word "unhappy" changes the meaning of "happy" to mean', 'Very happy', 'Not happy', 'Happy again', 'More happy', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Adding the suffix "-less" to the word "care" creates the word "careless," which means', 'Full of care', 'Without care', 'To take care', 'More careful', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, 'The word "gigantic" means very, very large. In the sentence "The gigantic elephant walked slowly through the tall grass," you can guess its meaning from the context.', 'Based on the passage, what does "gigantic" most likely mean?', 'Very small', 'Very large', 'Very fast', 'Very quiet', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which sentence is a declarative sentence?', 'Close the door!', 'Where is my book?', 'The sun rises in the east.', 'What a beautiful day!', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which sentence is an interrogative sentence?', 'The dog is barking.', 'Is the dog barking?', 'Stop the dog from barking!', 'What a loud dog!', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which sentence is an imperative sentence?', 'Please close the window.', 'Is the window open?', 'The window is open.', 'What a big window!', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which sentence uses the past tense correctly?', 'She will walk to school tomorrow.', 'She walks to school every day.', 'She walked to school yesterday.', 'She is walking to school now.', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which sentence uses a possessive pronoun correctly?', 'That book is her''s.', 'That book is hers.', 'That book is she.', 'That book is herself.', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Noong unang panahon, may isang matsing na mayabang. Isang araw, nakita niya ang isang pagong na mabagal maglakad. Kinutya niya ito. Ngunit sa isang paligsahan, natalo siya ng pagong dahil sa sobrang pagmamataas niya.', 'Ano ang uri ng kwentong ito?', 'Alamat', 'Pabula', 'Talambuhay', 'Balita', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, 'Noong unang panahon, may isang matsing na mayabang. Isang araw, nakita niya ang isang pagong na mabagal maglakad. Kinutya niya ito. Ngunit sa isang paligsahan, natalo siya ng pagong dahil sa sobrang pagmamataas niya.', 'Ano ang naging dahilan ng pagkatalo ng matsing?', 'Masyado siyang mabagal', 'Sobra siyang mayabang', 'Natulog siya sa daan', 'Hindi siya sumali sa paligsahan', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Ang isang alamat ay kwento tungkol sa', 'Kasalukuyang balita sa telebisyon', 'Pinagmulan ng isang bagay o lugar', 'Buhay ng isang tunay na tao', 'Talaan ng mga numero', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Sa isang maikling kwento, ang pangunahing tauhan ay tinatawag na', 'Simula', 'Aral', 'Pangunahing tauhan', 'Tagpuan', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Ang lugar at panahon kung saan naganap ang kwento ay tinatawag na', 'Tagpuan', 'Banghay', 'Aral', 'Tauhan', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Alin sa mga sumusunod ang halimbawa ng payak na pangungusap?', 'Kumain ako ng almusal at naligo rin ako.', 'Kumain ako ng almusal.', 'Kumain ako ng almusal, ngunit hindi ako naligo.', 'Kumain ako ng almusal kaya''t hindi ako nagutom.', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Ang tambalang pangungusap ay binubuo ng', 'Isang salita lamang', 'Dalawa o higit pang payak na pangungusap na pinagsama', 'Tanong lamang', 'Isang bantas lamang', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Alin sa mga sumusunod ang halimbawa ng tambalang pangungusap?', 'Maganda ang bulaklak.', 'Umuulan.', 'Umuulan, kaya''t nagdala ako ng payong.', 'Ang bulaklak.', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Ang salitang "malaki" ay kasingkahulugan ng', 'Maliit', 'Malawak', 'Mabilis', 'Mahina', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Ang salitang "mabilis" ay kasalungat ng', 'Mabagal', 'Malakas', 'Maliksi', 'Matulin', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Ang "malinis" at "malinaw" ay dalawang salita na parehong nangangahulugang', 'Magkasalungat sa isa''t isa', 'Walang kaugnayan sa isa''t isa', 'Malapit sa kahulugan ng "maayos"', 'Kasingkahulugan ng "marumi"', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Ang kasabihang "Aanhin pa ang damo kung patay na ang kabayo" ay isang halimbawa ng', 'Bugtong', 'Salawikain', 'Tula', 'Awit', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Ang isang bugtong ay karaniwang naglalaman ng', 'Isang aral tungkol sa buhay', 'Isang palaisipan na may sagot', 'Isang balita', 'Isang listahan ng pangalan', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Ang salawikain ay ginagamit upang', 'Magbigay ng payo o aral gamit ang matalinhagang pananalita', 'Magbalita ng kasalukuyang pangyayari', 'Magbilang ng mga numero', 'Magturo ng gramatika lamang', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Alin sa mga sumusunod ang wastong baybay?', 'paalaralan', 'paaralan', 'paralan', 'paaaralan', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Alin sa mga sumusunod ang wastong baybay ng salitang tumutukoy sa unang kain sa umaga?', 'almusal', 'almosal', 'almusar', 'almosar', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Alin sa mga sumusunod ang tamang baybay ng salitang tumutukoy sa lugar na pinagbibilhan?', 'palengki', 'palengke', 'palenke', 'palingke', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Alin sa mga sumusunod ang tamang gamit ng salitang "po" sa pangungusap?', 'Salamat po sa inyong tulong.', 'Po salamat sa inyong tulong.', 'Salamat sa inyong po tulong.', 'Salamat sa inyong tulong po po.', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which type of clouds are thin, wispy, and found high in the sky, often signaling fair weather?', 'Cirrus clouds', 'Nimbus clouds', 'Stratus clouds', 'Storm clouds', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these animals has fur as its body covering?', 'A parrot', 'A goldfish', 'A cat', 'A lizard', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these best describes an amphibian''s habitat during its life cycle?', 'It lives only in the air its whole life', 'It often lives in water when young and on land as an adult', 'It lives only underground', 'It never touches water at all', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which sentence uses the future tense correctly?', 'She walked to school yesterday.', 'She will walk to school tomorrow.', 'She walks to school every day.', 'She is walking to school now.', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which sentence is an exclamatory sentence?', 'Is it raining outside?', 'Close the umbrella.', 'What a huge storm this is!', 'It is raining outside.', 'c'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these community roles is a producer, not a consumer?', 'A student buying school supplies', 'A fisherman catching and selling fish', 'A family eating dinner at home', 'A shopper buying rice at the market', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these is an example of a plant''s need, based on what it needs to grow?', 'A pot with a painted design', 'Sunlight and water', 'A name tag', 'A ribbon', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these best summarizes the main idea of a story about a boy who shares his lunch with a hungry classmate?', 'The boy was hungry all day', 'Sharing and kindness can help others', 'Lunchboxes are expensive', 'The classmate never went to school again', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'In a story, if a character studies hard every night, what can you predict will most likely happen on the test?', 'The character will probably do well', 'The character will forget everything', 'The test will be cancelled', 'The character will skip the test', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these best explains cause and effect: "The plant did not get water, so it wilted."', 'The plant wilted, which caused it to not get water', 'Not getting water caused the plant to wilt', 'Wilting and watering are unrelated events', 'The plant got too much water and wilted', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which sentence correctly uses a coordinating conjunction to join two ideas?', 'It was raining, so we stayed inside.', 'It was raining we stayed inside.', 'It was raining, we stayed inside.', 'It, was raining so we stayed inside.', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these words means almost the same as "tired"?', 'Exhausted', 'Energetic', 'Excited', 'Awake', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these words is the opposite of "open"?', 'Wide', 'Closed', 'Unlocked', 'Visible', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'The prefix "re-" in the word "replay" changes the meaning of "play" to mean', 'To play for the first time', 'To play again', 'To stop playing', 'To never play', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Adding the suffix "-ful" to the word "help" creates the word "helpful," which means', 'Without help', 'Full of help, or useful', 'To ask for help', 'Never helping', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these is a Philippine national symbol?', 'The eagle of the United States', 'The Philippine flag', 'The maple leaf', 'The cherry blossom', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, '"Bayanihan" is a Filipino value that best means', 'Working alone without help', 'Helping one another as a community', 'Competing to be first', 'Ignoring your neighbors', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these correctly describes a mixture, like soil and water stirred together?', 'A new material forms that cannot ever be separated', 'Two or more materials are combined but can often be separated again', 'It always turns into a gas', 'It always turns into a solid', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which simple machine would best help you split a piece of wood in half?', 'Pulley', 'Wedge', 'Wheel and axle', 'Screw', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'A ramp used to help move a heavy box up into a truck is an example of which simple machine?', 'Inclined plane', 'Pulley', 'Wedge', 'Wheel and axle', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which of these best shows understanding of the barangay system''s purpose?', 'It was a way to organize early Filipino communities under a leader', 'It was a type of boat used for fishing', 'It was a school subject taught today', 'It was a type of clothing', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Which sentence best shows a child''s responsibility at home?', 'Deciding what the whole family eats every day', 'Helping to keep their room clean and tidy', 'Paying for the household''s electricity', 'Managing the family''s savings', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Kapag pinagsama ang dalawang payak na pangungusap gamit ang salitang "at," ito ay nagiging', 'Payak na pangungusap', 'Tambalang pangungusap', 'Tanong na pangungusap', 'Padamdam na pangungusap', 'b'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Ang salitang "masaya" ay kasalungat ng', 'Malungkot', 'Maligaya', 'Masigla', 'Matuwa', 'a'),
  (1, true, 3, NULL, 'Sa isang alamat, karaniwang ipinaliliwanag ang', 'Kasalukuyang balita', 'Pinanggalingan o dahilan ng isang bagay sa kalikasan', 'Talaan ng mga guro', 'Resulta ng isang laro', 'b');